<p>
James Cherti has announced <a href="https://www.jamescherti.com/emacs-org-ibullets/">a simple package that trades Org mode&rsquo;s heading stars for UTF-8 bullets</a>. If you&rsquo;re like me, your first thought is, &ldquo;Doesn&rsquo;t that already exist?&rdquo; Sort of. What already exists is the no longer maintained <a href="https://github.com/sabof/org-bullets">org-bullets</a>. Cherti&rsquo;s package is called <a href="https://github.com/jamescherti/org-ibullets.el">org-ibullets</a> (note the <code>i</code>).
</p>
<p>
Cherti explains the differences from org-bullets in his announcement. The TL;DR is that he&rsquo;s optimized org-ibullets by eliminating redundant computations, eliminated spurious syntax warnings that org-bullets could produce, and made some improvements at the source level.
</p>
<p>
As I said, the package is simple. It can be used right out of the box but you can customize the list of bullets and their face if you desire. This seems like a very nice package if you&rsquo;d like to make your Org buffers look a little nicer.</p>
